@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:architecture] preparation-and-raw-import-native-boundaries
Foliage preparation-only palette export, variant construction and snapshot helpers MUST remain outside
the native role-certification dependency used by unrelated raw mesh imports. Each consumer MUST bind the
compiled modules and saved types it actually executes or serializes. A preparation-module fix MUST NOT
be hidden by a synthetic unchanged module token, nor broaden raw import identity without a real dependency.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] saved-type-moves-preserve-native-compatibility
Moving a serialized class or struct between modules MUST preserve its intended fields/defaults and
provide the required old-path redirects. Source equivalence or a successful compile alone MUST NOT be
claimed as old-package compatibility: an existing saved asset MUST load through the redirects and its
runtime consumer MUST be validated before that compatibility is accepted.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] native-snapshot-is-the-saved-corner-stream
Native mesh snapshots MUST read the saved source mesh descriptions and match the versioned expected
stream's LOD/triangle/slot order and float32 corner positions, normals, colours and every UV channel.
Missing attributes, nonfinite data or unsupported shared/rewired topology MUST refuse. Bounds, triangle
counts and render-buffer similarity MUST NOT substitute for this proof. Readback MUST NOT mutate or save
the mesh; materials, build/LOD settings and source bindings still require their independent current checks.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:performance] foliage-json-allocation-lifetimes
Foliage variant construction MUST avoid an unnecessary full source-text copy when transferring owned
JSON text to its reader. Parsed root/level JSON objects MUST be released after conversion and before
building the mesh descriptions into the asset, once no remaining computation reads them. A lifetime
change MUST preserve the geometry/settings stream and MUST NOT free the descriptions needed by the build.
